                <pb facs="1335" n="1177" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1177"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 33.—<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bankruptcy law</hi>.</head>
                <p>The sentence of bankruptcy involves that all judicial distraint on any portion of
                    the property of the debtor, instituted prior to the bankruptcy, terminates
                    immediately, and that also from that moment no sentence respecting personal
                    detention can be executed.</p>
                <p>If the debtor is in prison he shall be liberated as soon as the sentence relating
                    to declaration of bankruptcy has taken effect, provided article 97 be
                    applied.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
